# Dynamic Edge — senior UI/UX + performance review

## 1. Brutal visual critique — **4/10**

The radial idea is recognizable, but the screenshot looks like a dark pie chart full of unrelated floating buttons. In "'`shot_quick`, faint wedge tiles, two circles per toggle (button plus icon), red slider, red glow, outer border, X and page marker all compete. Turn the bands off by default or reduce them to hairline separators; the nearly black low-contrast wedges currently make the layout look muddy. The red-to-brown gradient is conspicuous against the otherwise monochrome controls. The settings app exposes accent, rim, glow, bands and idle styles (`MainActivity.kt:88-102`), but these options multiply visual noise instead of defining a coherent theme.

Everything is technically radial, but not everything reads as a quarter-circle system: icons sit on independent round pucks inside pie slices. The slider is a broad outer arc, its small thumb is the only obvious affordance, and “brightness” has no icon/label. In `shot_media`, title/artist run diagonally on tight arcs and compete with the art and playback controls; absent media is especially awkward (“Not playing / Tap play to resume”). APPS icons appear scattered on white discs with no edit/remove cue. The white X button is a large, high-contrast dead-end at the bean centroid; dots sit so close that they read as part of the close control, and 2.5 dp dots are too subtle as page feedback (`EdgeView.kt:1226-1280`). The idle `dot` is barely a fingerprint on white backgrounds; `shot_idle` mostly shows home-screen icons, and the black bean blends into black wallpaper. Add a subtle edge/handle contrast and preview idle modes on both dark and light backgrounds.

Touch geometry is better than appearance: `itemRad` gives roughly 40 dp targets plus hit slop, but close’s visual radius is only 17 dp (`EdgeView.kt:640-645, 1581-1600`). Target 48 dp visually and semantically. The settings screen is a long, text-heavy form of labels and sliders (`MainActivity.kt:70-160`), despite the owner’s “visual, almost no text” goal.

## 2. Interaction / feel — **5/10**

Horizontal swipes page, vertical-down closes, and diagonal motion is also used for resize; quick swipes beginning in the gesture corner compete with system navigation (skill notes Assistant and Home gesture conflicts). Paging only triggers after horizontal movement dominates (`EdgeView.kt:1613-29`), so diagonal swipes can feel ignored or become resize. Add explicit radial page affordance and tune a dead-zone; never hijack normal vertical scrolling/touch-through near the panel edge. The X and page dots lack labels/accessibility descriptions. Sliders have no haptic detents or clear current value/auto mode. The section-opening spring may feel lively, but user speed/bounce settings are not enough: validate motion at 60/90/120 Hz and under load; keep control response immediate and content motion restrained. The slider jump-to-zero bug is plausible: `handleUp` rereads persisted brightness right after the last write (`EdgeView.kt:1747-50`); system writes/observer can lag. Keep the thumb’s final drag value until a confirmed observer update, and throttle writes.

## 3. Efficiency + smoothness, ranked

1. **Brightness writes per drag event**: `applySlider` writes `Settings.System` as the finger moves (`EdgeView.kt:1569-78`; `Brightness.kt:60-78`), causing synchronous provider work and observer churn. Render thumb locally every frame; coalesce writes to ~30–60 Hz and commit on release.
2. **Visualizer defeats zero-idle-work**: visualizer uses its own Choreographer loop (`EdgeView.kt:364-402`) while idle music plays. That is continuous wake/render work contrary to the skill’s zero-idle-frame rule. Make it opt-in and measure battery; stop whenever hidden/screen off.
3. **Full-window invalidation for small changes**: state, touch and progress call `invalidate()` (`EdgeView.kt:811-31, 1578`). Cached section RenderNodes help (`1150-80`), but moving thumb/progress still redraws the view and shape. Separate dynamic overlays from static layers; keep no frame callbacks except active motion/progress/visualizer.
4. **Layer memory / repeated art bitmaps**: up to three compositing RenderNodes are retained while open (`1154-80`); album art is scaled and old bitmaps are left to GC (`MediaBridge.kt:276-96`), while app icons allocate bitmaps on each load (`AppShortcuts.kt:18-46`). Release promptly, reuse scaled art where safe, and size art to physical display needs.
5. `addBand` allocates arrays/Paths on every `layoutAll()` (`EdgeView.kt:596-17`): fine off the hot path, but cache/reuse if size/theme changes become frequent. Springs use double-precision trig/exp every animated frame (`Spring.kt:30-65`); probably not the bottleneck versus window traversal/GPU, so profile before optimizing.

## 4. Bugs / risks

- Brightness drag completion can restore stale `bLevel` (above); `wasAuto` is set but never used to restore automatic mode after manual adjustment (`Brightness.kt:17, 60-79`). Provide an explicit auto/manual control and don’t silently leave auto-brightness disabled.
- `AssistControl.disableCornerGesture()` changes secure settings on service start, but there is no restore path (`AssistControl.kt:19-30`). Don’t silently take over a user gesture; make opt-in and restore only a value the app changed.
- `TouchRegion` depends on hidden reflected APIs and falls back to the entire window if blocked (`TouchRegion.kt:88-123`), risking touch interception after an OS update.
- `QuickToggles` uses deprecated Wi-Fi/Bluetooth enable APIs (`QuickToggles.kt:182-207`). Target SDK 28 may preserve legacy behavior today, but this is fragile across Android/OEM releases and distribution policies. DND, ringer mode, brightness and secure-setting access have separate grants/failure modes; render unavailable/permission-needed states rather than optimistic state.
- The service handles windows-changed to hide around IME (`EdgeService.kt:127-31`); verify focus and IME transitions across OEM keyboards, rotation, split screen and lock screen. Skill explicitly says these scenarios are not yet device-tested.

## 5. Top 10 feature ideas (ranked)

1. **QUICK editor**: visual radial preview with fixed angular slots, drag tile catalog into slots, reorder by angular position, empty slots, undo/reset. Persist ordered slot IDs, ring ID and angle; snap to equal-angle positions within each ring so every layout stays radial. Keep ring count/radius constrained by touch target and open size; show overflow pages, not tiny icons.
2. **Configurable control arc(s)**: choose brightness, media volume, ring volume, alarm volume, or no slider; allow 1–3 arcs with distinct icons/color and a selection ring. Use `AudioManager` stream volume APIs; respect DND/ringer restrictions. Add brightness auto toggle separately. Keep large arcs independently touchable and avoid crossing tile hit zones.
3. **Clipboard section**: radial outer arc of recent text snippets, inner focus/clipboard actions; center shows selected preview. Long-press pins, swipe-to-delete, clear history, per-item privacy. Use `ClipboardManager` plus `ACTION_PASTE` on the focused `AccessibilityNodeInfo` after placing text on clipboard; clipboard reads are restricted/background-sensitive, paste may fail for secure fields, apps without accessibility nodes, or apps that reject paste. Never promise universal paste; require deliberate accessibility enablement and disclose captured text retention.
4. Edit/remove/reorder APPS shortcuts in the same preview instead of the lone plus opening settings.
5. Add accessibility labels, keyboard/switch access, and scalable hit targets for every icon and arc.
6. Make idle affordance contrast adaptive to wallpaper brightness, with hide/opacity/edge inset controls.
7. Add per-tile long-press customization and clear permission/error states.
8. Add media output/device picker only where system APIs support it; maintain clear session ownership.
9. Add profiles (Work, Driving, Night) for quick layouts, accent and idle behavior.
10. Add measured low-power mode: disable idle visualizer, glow and nonessential animation; provide per-feature battery cost preview.

**Android limits:** `WRITE_SETTINGS` is user-approved special access for supported system settings. `WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS` is signature/privileged; ordinary users generally cannot grant it in Settings (ADB/root/device-owner/system-app routes are not normal consumer onboarding). Notification-listener access grants notification/media-session visibility, not arbitrary toggles. Accessibility permission does not grant blanket control of Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, GPS, mobile data or system panels. Use documented settings panels/intents when a toggle is restricted; disclose device/version differences. Secure settings such as global location are not safely writable just because an app is an accessibility service.

## 6. Single most important change

Build the visual radial QUICK editor and let it control a strict slot/ring model. It directly answers the product’s biggest unmet need—personalization—while forcing a coherent, legible layout instead of adding more fixed controls to an already crowded pie.
